        title = 'Prishe\'s Buddy',
        repeatable = 'No',
        previous = {'Flames in the Darkness'},
        next = {'Calm Before the Storm'},
        requirements = nil,
        walkthrough = '1. Travel to Mine Shaft #2716 and check the Shaft Entrance for a cutscene.\n   - There are several ways to reach this zone:\n     - Use the Home Point (Newton Movalpolos #1) - You should have this from when you came here for Promathia Mission 5-3.\n     - Trade a Snow Lily to Tarnotik at (K-10) in Oldton Movalpolos and he will warp you there.\n     - Gamble with Twinkbrix at (E-13) in Oldton Movalpolos until you win the [Key Item] Shaft 2716 operating lever, then pay him 2000 more gil to warp you there.\n     - The old fashioned (super-long) way of walking through Newton Movalpolos and operating the furnace hatches.\n     - This requires at least 3 people.\n2. Head to the Metalworks and speak with Cid.\n*Wait for a new Vana\'diel day and speak with Cid again to begin the next mission.',
        notes = '1. This was the last mission in the second CoP mission update.\n2. While Cid is repairing the airship, finishing Rise of the Zilart Missions is recommended to help understand the last chapters of this story.',
    },
    ['Flames for the Dead'] = {
        id = 568,
        start_npc = 'Hinaree',
        start_zone = 'Southern San d\'Oria',
        start_pos = 'A-6',
        description = 'Ulmia has journeyed to San d\'Oria to search for any word on the whereabouts of Prishe.',
        reward = nil,
        fame = nil,
        fame_level = nil,
        title = '*Delta Enforcer (defeating Mithra Sin Hunters)',
        repeatable = nil,
        previous = {'Three Paths'},
        next = {'For Whom the Verse Is Sung'},
        requirements = nil,
        walkthrough = '1. Note: If you did not already do so, speak with Cid (in Bastok - Metalworks - Home Point #1) to begin this Mission.\n2. Head to Southern San d\'Oria (A-6) (Home Point #4) and speak with Hinaree on the second floor of the manor for a short cutscene.\n\nEntanglement:\n\n3. Zone into Port San d\'Oria for a cutscene. Using the Home Point works.\n4. Speak with Chasalvige (L-6) in the Cathedral\'s Manuscript Room  in Northern San d\'Oria, left of the entrance.\n\nHead Wind:\n\n5. Travel to Windurst Waters (J-8) (Home Point #3) and speak with Kerutoto in the North wing of the Rhinostery. You may need speak with her more than once, as she offers other quests.\n      - The correct cutscene for this Mission is about you "standing there like a muddled mandragora" and of a girl with "crikey-spiky hair".\n6. Go to Windurst Walls (E-5) (Home Point #1) and speak with Yoran-Oran.\n7. Head to Attohwa Chasm (H-6), enter Boneyard Gully, and prepare for a boss fight.\n   - Home Point #1 in Attohwa Chasm or the Unity Warp (Level 125) will get you close to the entrance.\nWith the lifting of the level cap on this battlefield, this battle is now relatively trivial in difficulty. The walkthrough below was written for a level cap of 50.\n8. Some form of\n9. Food. MP and HP regen drinks\n10. Any other HP or MP potions\n11. Blackened Siredon (its usefulness is debatable)\n   - \'\'Note: Blackened Siredon is an item that is used to stop the Mithran Trackers TP gain for a short amount of time.\n     - If you wish to obtain these items, you need to complete the quest Mithran Delicacies given by Anguenet at (J-10) in Carpenters\' Landing. This quest is entirely optional.\'\'\n12. After your party is geared up and ready, click on the Dark Miasma and enter the battlefield "Head Wind". Buffs will wear off when you enter, so buff inside the battlefield.\n   - Read the battlefield names carefully; it is NOT the battlefield for "Like the Wind" if you happen to have that unlocked.\n      - They can each use their job specific abilities, spells, and more importantly Weaponskills with their respective weapons.\n      - They also tend to use skillchains and will team up accordingly.\n      - All the monsters in the battle have relatively low HP so they can be taken out fairly quickly with decent damage.\n      - The problem is their high TP gain and the ability to unleash devastating weaponskills.\n      - A well timed Sleepga at the start should allow everyone to take out one or more of the Mithran Trackers before the others awaken.\n      - Kill the pet\'s master before their corresponding pet, or they will summon another.\n      - Shikaree Y also Counters, so melees should attack her from the sides and back.\n      - Shikaree X and Shikaree Z have Utsusemi and Blink respectively.\n\nFlames for the Dead:\n\nWith the lifting of the level cap on this battlefield, this battle is now relatively trivial in difficulty. The walkthrough below was written for a level cap of 60.\n13. Icarus Wing, one for each melee.\n14. Opo-opo Necklace and Sleeping Potion, unless you can use Meditate\n15. Some form of\n16. A few Shu\'Meyo Salt.\n   - \'\'Note: Shu\'Meyo Salt is an item that delays the Snoll Tzar\'s explosion by 20 seconds.\n      - The Shu\'Meyo Salt takes away all hate when used, so if you have a PLD tank using 2hour, he should be last to use one, or not use any.\n         - This item may be obtained by completing the quest Bombs Away! given by Buffalostalker Dodzbraz at (F-9) in Uleguerand Range, and is highly recommended.\'\'\n17. Head to (J-9) of Uleguerand Range, jump into a hole on the ground and enter Bearclaw Pinnacle near Home Point #2.\n      - Closest warp is Home Point #2. The Unity warp 128 is probably the next best option if you don\'t have it.\n      - When your party is ready, click on the Wind Pillar and enter the battlefield "Flames for the Dead". Buffs will wear upon entering, so be sure to buff inside the battlefield.\n      - You may spend an extended time to buff you and your party, with melees building TP using Sleeping Potions with an Opo-opo Necklace, and/or using Meditate.\n      - When everyone is ready, pull the Snoll Tzar and unload everything you have on him, doing the most damage possible in the short amount of time by any means.\n18. It will use Hyperthermal Combustion 3 times throughout the battle, each one doing more damage than the last, making the snoll stronger in the process. The 3rd Hyperthermal Combustion ejects you from the battlefield.\n19. Arctic Impact: AoE ice damage (~275 each).\n20. Cold Wave: Nasty AoE Frost effect (31 HP/tick).\n21. Hiemal Storm: Extreme directional AoE ice damage for 200-1400 points.\n22. Berserk: Grants the Berserk effect. This makes the fight much easier, but is rare.\n   - The area attacks have a fairly small radius.\n      - The time limit in this battle is technically 30 minutes, although once you engage the Snoll Tzar you will have 45 seconds to defeat it before it ejects you from the battlefield.\n         - This time can be increased by using Shu\'Meyo Salt on it.\n         - Take care not to overlap the use of the salt because it will have no effect, wait for the message "The Snoll Tzar shakes off the salt!" before using the next one.\n      - Hiemal Storm also does quite a bit of damage so healers need to be on their toes during this fight. Don\'t hesitate to use Benediction if people are about to die!\n      - Popular 2 hours to use during this fight are Mighty Strikes, Hundred Fists, Meikyo Shisui, and Astral Flow.\n23. After you defeat the Snoll Tzar, return to Bastok and speak to Cid in the Metalworks again to finish this path.\n----\n24. If you have completed the other 2 paths (Louverance\'s Path, Tenzen\'s Path), Cid will give an additional cutscene and you can move on to the next Chapter: For Whom the Verse is Sung.\n\nOptional:\n\n25. After completing the battlefield, you\'ll be near the top of the mountain: register Home Point #1 by crossing the frozen pond (H-8).\n26. Out of the Depths is available in the Metalworks from Ayame (K-7) at the cannonry.\n   - In Oldton Movalpolos, a Moblin Hotrok can be obtained for the next quest.\n27. A Squire\'s Test, The Trader in the Forest, A Squire\'s Test II, and The Medicine Woman (level 20+) are pre-requisites for a Uleguerand Range quest, Over the Hills and Far Away (level 50+).\n   - \'Over the Hills and Far Away\' can be progressed in tandem with the next section, Flames for the Dead.\n   - Ahriman Tears x1 can be obtained in Uleguerand Range for a later quest.\n   - Snow Lily can also be obtained from Uleguerand Tigers there, if desired for Louverance\'s Path.',
        notes = nil,
    },
